  "id": "Compound::DB01174 - Gene::1548",
  "verbalization": "Phenobarbital exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c18 and Cyp2e1, which are both involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This binding likely influences the enzymatic activity of these cytochrome P450 proteins, which in turn modulate the activity of Cyp2a6. The shared involvement of Cyp2c18 and Cyp2e1 in arachidonic acid metabolism suggests a potential mechanism by which Phenobarbital indirectly affects Cyp2a6. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Phenobarbital may influence the expression or activity of Cyp2a6 through its interaction with these enzymes, potentially altering the metabolic pathways of arachidonic acid. The consistent involvement of Cyp2a6 in the metabolic processes of arachidonic acid, as observed across the paths, supports the notion that Phenobarbital exerts a regulatory effect on Cyp2a6 through these intermediary enzymes.",
